invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify.c
catches: p256_verify_equiv_test
reason: the host verifier takes u2*Q for R and leaves u1*G out of the sum,
  so it accepts only a signature whose hash is zero modulo n.
  bin/p256_verify_equiv_test requires the 32-bit verifier's verdict on
  every signature it tries.

--- old
    p256_wide_point_add(&sum, &sum, &addend);
--- new
    sum = addend;
